{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/848704-how-to-split-dice","id":848704,"title":"How to Split Dice?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-17T03:36:01-07:00","id":848704,"title":"How to Split Dice?","content":"Hello, I am currently directing a CTD game, and O wanted to update rules to 20th anniversary rules. There are 2 different approach on w20 and there is no good example in m20. Could you please explain it with examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T05:51:07-07:00","id":848734,"title":"","content":"I suggest you either use the old mechanics or wait on C20 to be finished.<br /> <br /> The old method was choose to do X actions, then take X actions, first at -(x+1)dice, second at -(x+2)dice, etc...<br /> <br /> W20 isn't sure if it wants the old mechanism or the new one :P<br /> <br /> The method in V20 and M20 is that you can do multiple actions by taking the lowest dicepool of all the actions that you want to do and then spread that single dicepool on any number of actions (i.e. you want to hack a computer while dodging bullets, your int+computers is 6 and your dex+athletics is 5, so you have to spread 5 dice on the hacking attempt and the dodge attempt). Note that this system is intended for different actions, because it actually breaks the game if you can use it on multiple attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T05:56:38-07:00","id":848737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/848704-how-to-split-dice?p=848734#post848734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suggest you either use the old mechanics or wait on C20 to be finished.<br /> <br /> The old method was choose to do X actions, then take X actions, first at -(x+1)dice, second at -(x+2)dice, etc...<br /> <br /> W20 isn't sure if it wants the old mechanism or the new one :P<br /> <br /> The method in V20 and M20 is that you can do multiple actions by taking the lowest dicepool of all the actions that you want to do and then spread that single dicepool on any number of actions (i.e. you want to hack a computer while dodging bullets, your int+computers is 6 and your dex+athletics is 5, so you have to spread 5 dice on the hacking attempt and the dodge attempt). Note that this system is intended for different actions, because it actually breaks the game if you can use it on multiple attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I want to shoot twice at one turn what should I do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T06:14:00-07:00","id":848744,"title":"","content":"The 2nd edition method of splitting a Dice Pool was to declare your actions (in your example shooting twice) take the lowest dice pool of the actions declared and literally split those dice into the actions. So if your Dex + Firearms was 6 and you wanted to shoot twice you could do two shots at 3 dice or one shot at 4 dice and one shot at 2 dice or one shot at 1 dice and one shot at 5 dice. Any combination that adds up to the 6 dice. If you wanted to shoot and do something else where the dice pool for Something Else was say only 4 dice, then you would be dividing 4 dice between the actions. <br /> <br /> One of the Revised methods was declare you actions. Your first action uses the dice pool of the action minus #of actions, the second action would deduct (#of actions +1) and so forth. So two shots would be dice pool 6 - 2(for actions declared) for 4 and second shot would be dice pool 6 - (2+1) for 3 dice. <br /> <br /> Vampire the Dark Ages introduces a new method in which you simpley declare that you are splitting actions, this incurs a cumulative -1 die +1 diff penalty. So action #1 loses 1 die from the dice pool and the diff goes up by 1, action #2 loses 2 dice and the diff goes up by 2. This means that it's easier to take defensive actions but makes it hard to do lots of things. It also introduces the concept of only 1 attack per round unless using extra actions granted by supernatural means (or two weapon wielding which makes the off hand penalty that's always been around actually mean something). Extra action powers allow for multi actions by reducing the penalties = to power level (or for something like Quicksilver # such is a good translation) and granting 1/2 the power level in extra actions allowed for attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T06:21:03-07:00","id":848746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KokoroWatari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/848704-how-to-split-dice?p=848737#post848737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I want to shoot twice at one turn what should I do?</div> </div> </div> </div>In which system :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T23:32:46-07:00","id":849166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/848704-how-to-split-dice?p=848744#post848744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 2nd edition method of splitting a Dice Pool was to declare your actions (in your example shooting twice) take the lowest dice pool of the actions declared and literally split those dice into the actions. So if your Dex + Firearms was 6 and you wanted to shoot twice you could do two shots at 3 dice or one shot at 4 dice and one shot at 2 dice or one shot at 1 dice and one shot at 5 dice. Any combination that adds up to the 6 dice. If you wanted to shoot and do something else where the dice pool for Something Else was say only 4 dice, then you would be dividing 4 dice between the actions. <br /> <br /> One of the Revised methods was declare you actions. Your first action uses the dice pool of the action minus #of actions, the second action would deduct (#of actions +1) and so forth. So two shots would be dice pool 6 - 2(for actions declared) for 4 and second shot would be dice pool 6 - (2+1) for 3 dice. <br /> <br /> Vampire the Dark Ages introduces a new method in which you simpley declare that you are splitting actions, this incurs a cumulative -1 die +1 diff penalty. So action #1 loses 1 die from the dice pool and the diff goes up by 1, action #2 loses 2 dice and the diff goes up by 2. This means that it's easier to take defensive actions but makes it hard to do lots of things. It also introduces the concept of only 1 attack per round unless using extra actions granted by supernatural means (or two weapon wielding which makes the off hand penalty that's always been around actually mean something). Extra action powers allow for multi actions by reducing the penalties = to power level (or for something like Quicksilver # such is a good translation) and granting 1/2 the power level in extra actions allowed for attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not understand the last part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T02:05:14-07:00","id":849183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KokoroWatari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/848704-how-to-split-dice?p=849166#post849166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did not understand the last part.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the system in DA:V20. Essentially, you say that you are splitting your actions, and say how many you will take. Then you take each action in its order and lower your dicepool by 1 and increase the difficulty by one. So let's say you want to do Three actions?<br /> <br /> Shoot a guy in the face, rip the suitcase from someone's hands and whack another guy in the face with the suitcase.<br /> Let's assume your Str, Dex, Firearms, Athletics and Brawl are all 2, and that your difficulty is 6<br /> <br /> You shoot the guy in the face with your Dex + Firearms (-1 dice +1 difficulty) - roll 3 dice at difficulty 7<br /> You grab the suitcase with your Str + Athletics (-2 dice +2 difficulty) - roll 2 dice at difficulty 8<br /> You whack someone in the face with Dex + Brawl (-3 dice +3 difficulty) - roll 1 dice at difficulty 9<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T09:48:14-07:00","id":849316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/848704-how-to-split-dice?p=849183#post849183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's the system in DA:V20. Essentially, you say that you are splitting your actions, and say how many you will take. Then you take each action in its order and lower your dicepool by 1 and increase the difficulty by one. So let's say you want to do Three actions?<br /> <br /> Shoot a guy in the face, rip the suitcase from someone's hands and whack another guy in the face with the suitcase.<br /> Let's assume your Str, Dex, Firearms, Athletics and Brawl are all 2, and that your difficulty is 6<br /> <br /> You shoot the guy in the face with your Dex + Firearms (-1 dice +1 difficulty) - roll 3 dice at difficulty 7<br /> You grab the suitcase with your Str + Athletics (-2 dice +2 difficulty) - roll 2 dice at difficulty 8<br /> You whack someone in the face with Dex + Brawl (-3 dice +3 difficulty) - roll 1 dice at difficulty 9</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. I understand it now. Is dexterity limiting factor? Do you suggest m20 system (which is the most recent one) or this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T16:11:18-07:00","id":849497,"title":"","content":"DA V20 is actually the most recent. But I still use the old Revised system personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T09:41:10-07:00","id":850156,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I think the not-splitting mechanic can be found somewhere in <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/89815/Dark-Ages-Basic-Rules?manufacturers_id=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T04:26:12-07:00","id":850489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/848704-how-to-split-dice?p=850156#post850156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I think the not-splitting mechanic can be found somewhere in <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/89815/Dark-Ages-Basic-Rules?manufacturers_id=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong Dark Ages book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T09:36:39-07:00","id":850620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon 