of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T19:33:10-07:00","id":852189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/848704-how-to-split-dice?p=848734#post848734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suggest you either use the old mechanics or wait on C20 to be finished.<br /> <br /> The old method was choose to do X actions, then take X actions, first at -(x+1)dice, second at -(x+2)dice, etc...<br /> <br /> W20 isn't sure if it wants the old mechanism or the new one :P<br /> <br /> The method in V20 and M20 is that you can do multiple actions by taking the lowest dicepool of all the actions that you want to do and then spread that single dicepool on any number of actions (i.e. you want to hack a computer while dodging bullets, your int+computers is 6 and your dex+athletics is 5, so you have to spread 5 dice on the hacking attempt and the dodge attempt). Note that this system is intended for different actions, because it actually breaks the game if you can use it on multiple attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the new old method, from Revised editions of the WoD (1998-2004). The old, old method (in the earlier editions, 1991-1998) relied on determining your lowest pool among all declared actions and dividing that sum among those actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T01:56:20-07:00","id":852288,"title":"","content":"Newoldoldnewold.<br /> <br /> I do remember that it was different and that I didn't like the original one, and that when I saw the revised one I used it for all the games hence. It's cute that Werewolf 20 has the lowest dicepool thing and variant of revised in it (with number of actions dicepool penalties, rather then number of actions +1)<br /> <br /> I vaguely remember that the limit on the 2nd editions was that you couldn't do the same action multiple times, but since I'm at work and the books are not around, do you remember if it was explicit there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}